From f8504332a632da22510d7b695ef732db248bb60e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 15:13:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0277 -- #10 UX: overlay reads "Rendering music...
 please wait"

Operator UX request against the first-launch organya precache overlay.

"Rendering music (one time)..." leads with an implementation detail the
player has no way to act on. "(one time)" is our jargon for "the PCM cache
persists across reboots" -- to someone staring at a progress bar on a
Pentium it reads as a shrug, not as guidance. What the player actually
needs to know at that moment is that the wait is expected and the machine
has not hung: on the POD-83 reference box the cold precache measures ~19
min / 47 MB across all 41 songs, which is long enough that "is it stuck?"
is the honest first reaction. "please wait" answers that; the ~19-min cost
is already explained where a player can read it up front (the SETUP music
description) rather than mid-render with nothing to do about it.

One string, both overlays. _oc_draw_progress is the single renderer for
BOTH the first-launch batch precache (main.cpp:2060, coarse song N/M bar +
the 0276 ESC-skip hint) and the in-game on-demand cold render of a single
song (per-beat callback, main.cpp:1486). The new text is correct in both:
it makes no claim about batching, count, or one-time-ness, so unlike
"(one time)" it does not misdescribe the in-game single-song case (where
the render is genuinely one-time for THAT song but the phrasing invited
the reading "this whole wait happens once ever").

Layout is unchanged: line1 is centered from Font::getWidth, and at 29
chars the new string is well inside the 320px overlay -- the 0276 ESC-skip
hint on the same screen is already 43 chars.

Text-only: no new env var, no new boot banner, no gate regex greps the old
string.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index c90b92fd..c627dd5e 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -1412,7 +1412,7 @@ static void _oc_draw_progress(uint32_t cur_beat, uint32_t total_beats)
   r->clearScreen(0, 0, 0);
   _oc_step("after clearScreen");
 
-  const char *line1 = "Rendering music (one time)...";
+  const char *line1 = "Rendering music... please wait";
   r->font.draw((W - (int)r->font.getWidth(line1)) / 2, H / 2 - 30, line1, 0xFFFFFF, true);
   _oc_step("after font.draw line1");
 
